  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN RCO Pemba office</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UN RCO Pemba office</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den svenska ambassaden i Mo&#xe7;ambique har mottagit ett f&#xf6;rslag fr&#xe5;n UN Resident Coordinators Office (RCO) f&#xf6;r att&#xa0;finansiera en Nexus-koordinatorpost och en FN-volont&#xe4;rpost (UNV) med placering i Pemba, huvudstad i provinsen Cabo Delgado under tv&#xe5; &#xe5;r med m&#xf6;jlighet till f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning.

Insatsens m&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttning &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra utvecklingseffektiviteten genom samordning mellan humanit&#xe4;ra och l&#xe5;ngsiktiga utvecklings&#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder, s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l som mellan FN-organ, andra utvecklingsakt&#xf6;rer och med staten p&#xe5; olika niv&#xe5;er.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Embassy in Mozambique has received a proposal from the UN Resident CoordinatorsOffice (RCO) to fund a Nexus Coordinator post and a United Nations Volunteer post to be placed in Pemba, the Cabo Delgado provincial capital, under the realm of the RCO. It is be a two-year post with possibility for extension.

The intervention&apos;s main objective is to improve development effectiveness through coordination between humanitarian and long term development actions, as well as between UN agencies and with government.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initial purpose of this contribution was to support the RCO Pemba office with a number of staff positions, including a P5 nexus position during a two year period with the purpose of enhancing coordination between recovery, peace and development in Cabo Delgado. Due to shortcomings in the recruitment process, it was decided to reduce and reshape the support to a one year agreement with support to a national level Maputo-based coordination position. This coordination function will mainly support the DCP secretariat (Development Cooperation Platform), and the two DCP chairs (Sweden and the RCO), but also offer support to the RCO office and RC/HC in general.</narrative>
  </description>
